READING: M(v^N) rises toward M(U) from below; the gap shrinks ~ L/(2N).
The bound is ELEMENTARY (Lipschitz F + 1/(2N)-dense rational-slope curve) --
NO Jain-Kravitz lift-limit theorem.  So the (A)-subsumption stands on:
  (i) M(v^N) <= M(U) [trivial], (ii) |M(v^N)-M(U)| <= L/2N [this, elementary],
  (iii) opus residue bridge [formal], (iv) finite census [the open crux].
